#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:4
msgid "Debugging Syncthing"
msgstr "除錯 Syncthing"

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:6
msgid ""
"There's a lot that happens behind the covers, and Syncthing is generally "
"quite silent about it. A number of environment variables can be used to set "
"the logging to verbose for various parts of the program, and to enable "
"profiling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:11
msgid ""
"Under Unix (including Mac) the easiest way to run Syncthing with an "
"environment variable set is to prepend the variable to the command line. I.e:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:15
msgid "``$ STTRACE=model syncthing``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:17
msgid "On windows, it needs to be set prior to running Syncthing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:21
msgid ""
"C:\\> set STTRACE=model\n"
"C:\\> syncthing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:25
msgid "Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../includes/env-vars.rst:1
msgid "STTRACE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../includes/env-vars.rst:2
msgid ""
"Used to increase the debugging verbosity in specific facilities, generally "
"mapping to a Go package. Enter a comma-separated string of facilities to "
"trace: ``api,beacon``. Optionally, a log level can be given per facility to "
"specify something other than DEBUG: ``api:WARN,beacon:ERR``, potentially "
"overriding a global ``--log-level`` adjustment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../includes/env-vars.rst:9
msgid ""
"The valid facility strings are listed below; additionally, ``syncthing serve "
"--help`` always outputs the most up-to-date list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../includes/env-vars.rst:12
msgid ""
"api             - REST API beacon          - Multicast and broadcast "
"discovery config          - Configuration loading and saving connections     "
"- Connection handling db/sqlite       - SQLite database dialer          - "
"Dialing connections discover        - Remote device discovery "
"events          - Event generation and logging fs              - Filesystem "
"access main            - Main package model           - The root hub "
"nat             - NAT discovery and port mapping pmp             - NAT-PMP "
"discovery and port mapping protocol        - The BEP protocol relay/"
"client    - Relay client scanner         - File change detection and hashing "
"stun            - STUN functionality syncthing       - Main run facility "
"upgrade         - Binary upgrades upnp            - UPnP discovery and port "
"mapping ur              - Usage reporting versioner       - File versioning "
"watchaggregator - Filesystem event watcher"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../includes/env-vars.rst:36
msgid "STLOCKTHRESHOLD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../includes/env-vars.rst:37
msgid ""
"Used for debugging internal deadlocks; sets debug sensitivity. Use only "
"under direction of a developer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../includes/env-vars.rst:40
msgid "STVERSIONEXTRA"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../includes/env-vars.rst:41
msgid ""
"Add extra information to the version string in logs and the version line in "
"the GUI. Can be set to the name of a wrapper or tool controlling syncthing "
"to communicate this to the end user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../includes/env-vars.rst:45
msgid "GOMAXPROCS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../includes/env-vars.rst:46
msgid ""
"Set the maximum number of CPU cores to use. Defaults to all available CPU "
"cores."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../includes/env-vars.rst:49
msgid "GOGC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../includes/env-vars.rst:50
msgid ""
"Percentage of heap growth at which to trigger GC. Default is 100. Lower "
"numbers keep peak memory usage down, at the price of CPU usage (i.e. "
"performance)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../includes/env-vars.rst:54
msgid "LOGGER_DISCARD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../includes/env-vars.rst:55
msgid ""
"Hack to completely disable logging, for example when running benchmarks. Set "
"to any nonempty value to use it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:30
msgid "Stepping with breakpoints"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:32
msgid ""
"If you like to step through the running program, build a non-optimized "
"binary and run with  https://github.com/derekparker/delve."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:34
msgid "Follow these steps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:38
msgid ""
"$ go run build.go -debug-binary build\n"
"$ STNODEFAULTFOLDER=1 STNOUPGRADE=1  STNORESTART=1 dlv --listen=:2345 --"
"headless=true --api-version=2 exec ./syncthing -- --home=./_test_config --no-"
"browser"
msgstr ""
"$ go run build.go -debug-binary build\n"
"$ STNODEFAULTFOLDER=1 STNOUPGRADE=1  STNORESTART=1 dlv --listen=:2345 --"
"headless=true --api-version=2 exec ./syncthing -- --home=./_test_config --no-"
"browser"

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:41
msgid "For installing and using delve itself see:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:43
msgid ""
"VSCode (Microsoft): https://github.com/golang/vscode-go/blob/master/docs/"
"debugging.md"
msgstr ""

